  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Somaliland Country Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TradeMark Africa&apos;s Somaliland Programme works to unlock the trade potential of one of the Horn of Africa&apos;s most strategically positioned but underserved territories, operating since 2020 in partnership with the Government of Somaliland and the private sector along the Berbera Corridor, a route of growing regional significance connecting landlocked Ethiopia to the Port of Berbera. The Programme advances trade facilitation across five interconnected areas: strengthening the trade and investment environment through policy and regulatory reform aligned with regional frameworks; improving the quality and value of traded goods through standards and sanitary and phytosanitary capacity building in support of key export sectors including livestock, which dominates Somaliland&apos;s trade; advancing digital trade systems to modernise customs processes and reduce transaction costs; improving physical connectivity at key border and port infrastructure nodes; and promoting greener, more resilient, and inclusive trade with a deliberate focus on women traders and small-scale cross-border participants who have historically been excluded from formal trade channels.</narrative>
  </description>
